{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno5_js_face_recon",
    "description": "Pointwise classical (Jiang-Shu 1996) WENO5 reconstruction of a cell-averaged/point field at the face between the third and fourth cells of a five-cell window v0..v4 (cells i-2, i-1, i, i+1, i+2 for the face i+1/2, upwind-biased to the left): the three third-order candidate stencils f1 = (2 v0 - 7 v1 + 11 v2)/6, f2 = (-v1 + 5 v2 + 2 v3)/6, f3 = (2 v2 + 5 v3 - v4)/6 with linear weights 1/10, 3/5, 3/10, smoothness indicators beta_k = 13/12 (second difference)^2 + 1/4 (first-difference combination)^2, and the classical nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2 with eps = 1e-6 and power 2 -- NOT the WENO-Z weights of stencils/weno5_recon.esm on cartesian_uniform_1d, and NOT the Hamilton-Jacobi divided-difference form of hjweno_recon_*. eps = 1e-6 is the literal fire_behavior uses (TOL in Select_weno5), on the field's own value scale; it is not dimensionally scaled. Fifth order in smooth regions away from critical points, degrading to third order where a first derivative vanishes (the known Jiang-Shu limitation that WENO-Z repairs). Match-less helper of the weno5_eno1_* stencils of this grid; the mirrored (right-biased) face is obtained by binding the window in reverse order.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:reconstruct",
      "axes:x",
      "order:5",
      "stencil_width:5"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical WENO5 smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls, Select_eno, Select_weno5, Select_4th, Select_godunov (case 4), Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
